<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Souliote Confederacy</h1><p class="st-meta">1660 CE – 1803 CE (approx.) · capital Souli</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Self-governing community of Orthodox warrior clans in the mountains of Epirus, famous for resisting Ali Pasha of Ioannina for over a decade.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Souli was a group of villages in the rugged mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thesprotia">Thesprotia</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a>. From the mid-17th century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> Christian families, mainly Albanian-speaking, settled there and built a free community outside effective Ottoman control, growing into a confederation of villages such as Souli, Kiafa, Avariko and Samoniva.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Souliote society was organised in clans (fares), each with its own leader; a council of chiefs decided on war. Men were full-time warriors who lived from herding and from tribute imposed on surrounding villages; women also fought. Leading families included the Botsaris and Tzavelas. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/souliotes">Souliotes</a> spoke Albanian and Greek and were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-pasha-of-yanina">Ali Pasha of Ioannina</a> attacked repeatedly from 1792 and finally forced their surrender in December 1803. Many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/souliotes">Souliotes</a> went to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/corcyra">Corfu</a>, while women reportedly threw themselves from the cliffs at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dance-of-zalongo">Zalongo</a>. They returned to fight in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-war-of-independence">Greek War of Independence</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/markos-botsaris">Markos Botsaris</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/souliote-confederacy.jpg" alt="Souliote Confederacy" width="320" height="193"><figcaption>Image: Charles Robert Cockerell · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albanian_Palikars_in_pursuit_of_an_enemy_--_Charles_Robert_Cockerell,_1813-1814_--_British_Museum,_inv._1923,0113.30.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1660 CE – 1803 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Souli</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Georgios Botsaris, Lambros Tzavelas, Fotos Tzavelas</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Albanian, Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Souli, Confederation of Souli</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1732&amp;focus=souliote-confederacy" aria-label="Souliote Confederacy on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5205 780 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Souliote Confederacy lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5514 1013h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5525 1036h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5525 1036h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Greece. <a href="/atlas?year=1732&amp;focus=souliote-confederacy">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

